WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.919
The Evaluate phase asks whether the course worked and how it should improve.

2
00:00:04.919 --> 00:00:07.378
Evaluation happens in two broad ways.

3
00:00:07.378 --> 00:00:15.679
Formative evaluation occurs during design and development, when feedback can still shape the course before or during rollout.

4
00:00:15.679 --> 00:00:24.518
Summative evaluation occurs after delivery, when the team looks at course results, learner outcomes, and improvement opportunities.

5
00:00:24.518 --> 00:00:36.277
Formative evaluation can include storyboard reviews, prototype reviews, accessibility checks, usability tests, pilot feedback, SME feedback, and early learner observations.

6
00:00:36.277 --> 00:00:41.272
The purpose is to improve the course before the full audience experiences it.

7
00:00:41.272 --> 00:00:51.110
A confusing interaction, weak example, poor caption, or mismatched quiz question is much easier to fix before launch than after a compliance deadline.

8
00:00:51.110 --> 00:00:54.569
Summative evaluation uses evidence after delivery.

9
00:00:54.569 --> 00:01:07.327
Common signals include learner feedback, quiz results, completion data, LMS reports, support tickets, manager feedback, performance indicators, quality metrics, and workplace observation.

10
00:01:07.327 --> 00:01:08.864
Each signal has limits.

11
00:01:08.864 --> 00:01:15.397
Completion data tells you whether learners finished, but not necessarily whether they can perform.

12
00:01:15.397 --> 00:01:19.624
Quiz results may show recall, but not always workplace transfer.

13
00:01:19.624 --> 00:01:23.544
Useful evaluation looks beyond attendance and completion.

14
00:01:23.544 --> 00:01:33.459
If the course was meant to reduce errors, improve decisions, support compliance, or standardize a process, look for evidence connected to that outcome.

15
00:01:33.459 --> 00:01:37.148
Sometimes the evidence shows the course needs revision.

16
00:01:37.148 --> 00:01:45.372
Sometimes it shows the course is fine but the job environment needs better tools, clearer policies, or manager reinforcement.

17
00:01:45.372 --> 00:01:48.215
Evaluation should feed the next iteration.

18
00:01:48.215 --> 00:01:55.901
Capture what worked, what confused learners, what reviewers flagged, what data changed, and what updates are needed.

19
00:01:55.901 --> 00:02:02.895
ADDIE becomes a cycle when evaluation informs future analysis, design, development, and implementation.
